# /plan — Write an Implementation Plan

Read the approved `specs/<feature>/spec.md` and write a technical
implementation plan to `specs/<feature>/plan.md`.

## Instructions

1. Confirm `specs/<feature>/spec.md` exists and is approved
   (`sddkit approve <feature> spec` must have been run).
2. Write `specs/<feature>/plan.md` using the template below.
3. **Every REQ-NNN from the spec must be cited at least once in this plan.**
   The checker will flag any missing ones.
4. After writing, remind the user to run:
   ```
   sddkit check <feature>
   sddkit approve <feature> plan
   ```

## plan.md Template

```markdown
# Plan: <Feature Name>

## Summary
<!-- One paragraph technical summary of the approach. -->

## Architecture Changes
<!-- List files and modules that will be created or modified. -->

## Implementation Steps

### Step 1 — <title>
<!-- Description. REQ-NNN -->

### Step 2 — <title>
<!-- Description. REQ-NNN, REQ-NNN -->

## Data / Schema Changes
<!-- DB migrations, API schema changes, config changes. -->

## Dependencies
<!-- New libraries or services required. -->

## Risk & Mitigations
<!-- Potential failure modes and how they are handled. -->
```

## Constraints
- Do not reference any requirement not in `spec.md`.
- Do not begin writing tasks until the plan is approved.
